# Crash-injection DoD (plan §7/§8): kill the real process INSIDE the regen of
# a supersede — after constitution.md is written, before the manifest. Both
# ADR writes already committed; the projection files are pure derivations, so
# a following regen must parse the log and converge — "regen self-heals".

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02
env CONSTITUTION_CRASH_AFTER=after-projection

# The process is killed mid-sequence (exit 137, non-zero).
! exec constitution supersede ADR-0001 --title 'Replacement' --body-file body.md

# At this seam the new ADR exists but the old one is still accepted — a log
# that parses. Recovery is a plain regen, which must succeed (proving the log
# parses) and be idempotent.
env CONSTITUTION_CRASH_AFTER=
exec constitution regen
stdout 'wrote'
cp constitution/constitution.md first.md
exec constitution regen
cmp constitution/constitution.md first.md

-- constitution.yml --
schemaVersion: 1
phase: sealed
consent:
  policy: off
sourceTracking:
  type: none
categories:
  - architecture

-- constitution/adr/ADR-0001-original.md --
---
id: ADR-0001
title: Original
category: architecture
date: 2026-06-01
status: accepted
---

## Context and Problem Statement

x

## Considered Options

- a

## Decision Outcome

y

-- body.md --
